    "ratio_per_element_over_vectorised": 33.75,
    "per_element_loop_vectors_per_s": 10158.7,
    "note": "Per-element cost of the raw scalar draw is 0.128 us/element (measured), while the paper's 2339 vectors/s at d=768 corresponds to 428 us/vector = 0.56 us/element. A per-element Python implementation doing a handful of numpy-scalar operations per coordinate would land in that range, so the 'paper used a per-element-style implementation' statement is a plausible reconstruction (A17), NOT a measurement of the paper's code. This reproduction draws all d Gaussians with a single PCG64 call, hence the ~34x higher per-vector throughput."
